<p>In the latest development, human rights monitors said at least 70 people were killed and 30 wounded in a gang attack in Haiti’s Artibonite region, far above the initial official toll. The attack took place near Petite-Riviere in the Artibonite department, and rights groups said the violence also forced nearly 6,000 people to flee. The conflicting casualty counts underscore how hard it is to document attacks quickly in insecure areas. The new higher estimates, reported by the Defenseurs Plus rights group and echoed across several outlets, point to a broader humanitarian emergency in central Haiti as residents search for safety.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/1ePBeFoegQvq6CTNqMYzIIVh_5oTB4x4GWciqFo5hmLmdnE-jhB7qqhnjIBr9Df7uT0NCGFqGKWcJF01mkmsJM9AKDGBCUpUBK63NPpMIBEeHZRlJOxZ1uclHP2NTsg_iPEmMnW25Qvxk7-6mB5wXgvpIFWdh8sN4lxFDgs2vcIXTRVi5XdDvQ4VhKSU8UUu2PxxwqjzhQpmmxLVZjk94Cv92H4VemQnGMb_CqJsJskmfP7H7QRvX1Xj0A' alt='Haitian security forces patrol in Port-au-Prince, Haiti, February 6, 2026.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Repeat violence: ABC News reported that the gang had renewed its attack on the town, suggesting residents were struck more than once rather than in a single isolated assault.</li><li>Unaccounted for: Haitian activists told ABC News that dozens of people were still missing after the attack.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Defenseurs Plus: The Haitian rights group described the assault as a massacre and criticised what it called the abandonment of residents by authorities after the attack. (<a href='https://www.dw.com/en/haiti-at-least-70-killed-in-massacre-says-rights-group/a-76600042'>DW</a>, <a href='https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/mar/30/deaths-in-gang-attack-haitian-farming-area-far-exceed-initial-estimate'>The Guardian</a>)</li><li>Haitian police: Police initially reported 16 people killed and 10 injured after the attack, offering the first official assessment from the scene. (<a href='https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/mar/30/deaths-in-gang-attack-haitian-farming-area-far-exceed-initial-estimate'>The Guardian</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.lemonde.fr/en/international/article/2026/03/30/in-haiti-at-least-sixteen-dead-in-a-gang-attack_6751961_4.html'>In Haiti, at least 16 dead in a gang attack</a> - lemonde.fr</li><li><a href='https://www.dw.com/en/haiti-at-least-70-killed-in-massacre-says-rights-group/a-76600042'>Haiti: At least 70 killed in &#x27;massacre,&#x27; says rights group</a> - dw.com</li><li><a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/3/31/at-least-70-killed-30-wounded-in-haiti-gang-attack-rights-group-says'>At least 70 killed, 30 wounded in Haiti gang attack, rights group says</a> - aljazeera.com</li><li><a href='https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/mar/30/deaths-in-gang-attack-haitian-farming-area-far-exceed-initial-estimate'>At least 70 people killed and 30 injured in Haiti gang attack</a> - theguardian.com</li><li><a href='https://abcnews.com/International/wireStory/activists-haiti-30-people-dead-after-gang-attacks-131544611'>Activists in Haiti say at least 30 people are dead after a gang attacks a town again</a> - abcnews.com</li><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/at-least-16-dead-10-injured-in-haiti-town-police-says'>At least 70 killed in Haiti massacre, rights group says, far exceeding official toll</a> - straitstimes.com</li></ul>